rgest salt flat in the world, with an area of approximately 10,582 square kilometres (4,086 mi<sup>2</sup>). It is situated in southwestern Bolivia, within the Daniel Campos Province of the Potosí Department, near the crest of the Andes Mountains, at an elevation of 3,656 m (11,995 ft) above sea level.</p>"}